From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Fri, 19 Sep 2026 09:12:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a <webview> says when its page asks for a window

Three lists, so that the event a `<webview>` dispatches when its page asks for
a window of its own is compiled and reaches the page:
`core/html/build.gni` builds `DomicileNewWindowEvent`, `idl_in_core.gni`
generates its bindings, and `generated_in_core.gni` names the generated pair
for the build to compile.

Everything else this fix needs is new files, which `src/` carries: the event
itself, `HTMLWebViewElement::NewWindowRequested`, the `NewWindowRequested`
member on `WebViewGuestClient`, and the send in
`WebViewGuest::CreateCustomWebContents` that replaces a warning nobody could
act on. Before it, a link with `target="_blank"` inside a browser window did
nothing at all: the browser refuses the window content would have made -- a
guest has no SiteInstance of its own and content CHECKs that pair -- and until
now it refused it silently.

THE EVENT IS IN core/ RATHER THAN modules/, which is why this patch edits the
core lists rather than the module ones patch 0009 edits. The element that
dispatches it is a core element, and core cannot depend on modules. It carries
no `…EventInit` dictionary and no constructor for the same reason the
dictionary lists are untouched here: only the browser process makes one of
these, and a dictionary would be two more generated files in two more lists
for a constructor no shell calls.

THE POSITION IN EACH LIST is beside patch 0007's own entries, which is where
the fork's other core files went. `scripts/test-the-blink-module-declares-its-
files.sh` is what fails when a file under `core/html/domicile/` is missing from
either registry -- neither omission is a compile error, and the cost of finding
one out is an engine release.

THE POST-IMAGE BLOB HASHES ARE ZEROED, and that is a fact about where this was
written rather than a style. A hash is sha1 of the whole resulting file, and
this patch was made without a Chromium checkout to produce one from; the
PRE-image hashes are real, taken from patch 0007's post-image, so
`scripts/test-patch-series-chain.sh` still reads this as landing on the series
rather than on the bare pin. `git am` applies by context and never looks at
either. The first `extract.sh` after this lands on a real tree replaces both
with what the tree says.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium, and the guard that
measures the behavior end to end --
`packages/domicile-engine/scripts/guard-webview-new-window.sh`, a
`target="_blank"` link clicked in a browser window and the second `<webview>`
the shell opens for it -- runs on `crux` with the rest of the engine job.
